  "name": "Monthly and Annual Marine Weather for the Pacific Ocean",
  "description": "Publication Title: Marine Climatological Summaries. Includes monthly and annual means and extremes of dry-bulb temperature, dew-point temperature, sea temperature, pressure, and clouds; monthly and annual percentage frequency of visibility and of wind speed and direction; percentage frequency of wave height and direction; weather. Area covered ranges from 40-180 degrees W and from 55 degrees S-78 degrees N. A station location map is also included. Vol.1 (1961)-v.10(1970) available from the NOAA Library System: URL http://www.lib.noaa.gov/. Data for 1971- continued in digital form only by COADS project.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This publication is in the National Oceanic & Atmospheric Administration Library, and is one of many books, atlases, maps, charts and other printed materials received by NOAA from many nations over the years.",
